From 3939fc78bf5fecda485d7894f90cc6db63d3388d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:58:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(storage): expire failed named claims without deleting
 newer objects

Context:
Greptile P1 on d793036 noted that an unconditional R2.delete after a KV metadata failure can remove a newer generation if another request reclaimed the name first.

Expected behavior:
If this request still owns the claimed object, mark that generation expired so a retry can reclaim it. If a newer upload already replaced it, leave the newer object untouched.

Acceptance criteria:
- KV metadata failure still leaves the original name retryable
- a newer R2 generation written before cleanup survives the failed request

Constraints:
- generic upstream behavior only; no Feishu concepts
- do not modify upstream-sync

Validation:
- RED: worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts newer-generation case failed because R2.get returned null
- GREEN: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts -> 6 passed
- REGRESSION: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --project Workers -> 17 files, 120 tests passed
- tsc --noEmit and eslint on changed files passed

Docs:
- N/A; public API contract unchanged

Upstream base:
0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6

Patch ID:
050-atomic-named-paste-create (candidate; verify against refreshed series before export)

Dependencies:
none

Refs:
- https://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/issues/78
- https://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/pull/99
- Greptile P1 on d793036: cleanup deletes newer generation
